{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And give seed.</b> To sow the land. And even though Yosef said, ״and there are yet five years in which there shall be neither plowing nor harvest,״ once Yaakov came to Egypt, blessing came at his heels and they began to sow, and the famine ended — and so we learned in the Tosefta of Sotah." "<b>Let it not be.</b> Let it not lie desolate; לָא תְבוּר — a term for a fallow field, that is not plowed."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:49.817074666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}